Appendix G Additional Features
******************************

* Menu:

* kTLS (Kernel TLS)::


File: gnutls.info,  Node: kTLS (Kernel TLS),  Up: Additional Features

G.1 kTLS (Kernel TLS)
=====================

kTLS (Kernel TLS) is a Linux kernel feature that offloads TLS encryption
and decryption operations to the kernel space, improving performance and
reducing CPU overhead.  It allows applications to leverage zero-copy
data transmission, reducing context switches between user space and
kernel space.

The following table shows how to enable kTLS support on Linux and
FreeBSD systems.

Description                   Linux                  FreeBSD
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Load kernel module            ‘modprobe tls’         ‘kldload tls’
Check if module is loaded     ‘lsmod | grep tls’     ‘kldstat | grep tls’
kTLS rekey support            v6.14                  not yet supported

Table G.1: kTLS system enable

To enable ktls in GnuTLS *note Enabling kTLS::.


